  "deviations": [
    "Variants are Webflow component variants (styles only), named Base, Dark, Image Bg, Burgundy, Centered, not is- combo classes on the dialog.",
    "Content differences between instances are Show booleans and text props; an empty Image prop renders a broken image, so every instance sets Image (or Show image off).",
    "One list of five items serves three looks: numbered spec rows (Base), image cards with reserve buttons (Image Bg) and menu links (Burgundy, which shows only each item's button label).",
    "No global [data-modal-overlay] element: each dialog carries its own backdrop div with data-modal-close and data-modal-no-overlay on the root.",
    "Heading size follows the variant (h2 2.5rem on Base and Centered, h3 1.875rem on Dark), not a heading-style utility, because a variant cannot swap classes.",
    "arts/13 places the artwork caption in a second column next to the 'by' line; the component stacks eyebrow and caption under the heading.",
    "Image Bg and Burgundy have no visible heading in Figma; Show heading is off there, so those dialogs get no aria-labelledby. A page session can set an aria-label on the instance root later if needed."
  ],
